From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:53:46 +0200
Subject: nouveau: a submission the kernel fails counts as cancelled

The winsys counted only the submissions ps3rsx cancelled (-ECANCELED) in
nouveau_device::cancelled. A push buffer the kernel failed another way (an
-EINVAL or -ENOMEM from the pushbuf ioctl) did not get there either, but nothing
said so: its queries' reports never came, and a wait for one (nv30's, which gave
up on a lost report only on the PS3) ended nowhere. It now counts too, so its
queued words are dropped, the driver sends its state again before it draws and
the reports it held are taken as lost.

The count is bumped and read atomically (NOUVEAU_CANCEL, NOUVEAU_CANCELLED):
contexts of one screen submit from their own threads. nv30's query wait gives up
on a report whose submission did not go on every machine; its one second
deadline stays the PS3's.

A submission whose fence could not be made (kick_notify fails) counts too: its words stay in the push
buffer without their relocations, and the next kick drops them. The message and the dump of a failing
pushbuf ioctl come at the 1st, 2nd, 4th... failure, as for -ECANCELED.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
@@ -376,7 +376,7 @@ _nouveau_fence_wait(struct nouveau_fence *fence, struct util_debug_callback *deb
       /* ps3rsx cancelled the submission it was in (nouveau_device::cancelled): it never
        * lands. The next fence to land after it signals it: submit the context's current one
        * and wait for that (the kick drops what was queued on the lost state, not the fence). */
-      if (fence->state != NOUVEAU_FENCE_STATE_SIGNALLED && screen->device->cancelled &&
+      if (fence->state != NOUVEAU_FENCE_STATE_SIGNALLED && NOUVEAU_CANCELLED(screen->device) &&
           fence->context && fence->context->fence && fence->context->fence != fence) {
          struct nouveau_fence *next = NULL;
 
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h
@@ -269,7 +269,7 @@ nv30_state_lost(struct nv30_context *nv30);
